# The task-forest (`.agent-workbench/`) is the maintainer's PERSONAL orchestration
# scaffolding, not an engineering deliverable. The dev flow uses it locally, but a
# cloner does not need it — so the whole tree stays out of version control. Files
# remain on disk; nothing here is deleted. Product code, CI (`.gitlab-ci.yml`) and
# the shipped packages have zero dependency on it being tracked; `scripts/check-forest-landing.mjs`
# degrades to "cannot measure" (exit 2) when the forest is absent, by design.
# NOTE: this only stops FUTURE tracking. The ~85 MB of historical `events/events.jsonl`
# blobs already live in pushed history (111 commits) and still transfer on clone;
# removing that needs a history rewrite, which issue #27 / TF-0147 deliberately declined.
/.agent-workbench/
# local session work log + scratch scripts (tf-* probes, tmp-* exit codes,
# repin.py, scan reports) — personal workspace state, not repo history
/.workbuddy/
# ZCode agent-local scratch (session plans + test logs, e.g. .zcode/plans)
/.zcode/
# closeout scan rounds (integrity reports + test logs); curated findings are
# transcribed into docs/ reports and task-forest node evidence
/.agent-contexts/closeout-*/
/.agent-contexts/closeout-*.log
/.agent-contexts/issue-6-closeout-*/
# Audit raw fixtures and logs stay local; reviewed summaries live in docs/.
/.agent-contexts/audit-errors-*/
# 2026-09-16 integrity audit + fix round: same rule — raw probes/logs are local
# machine evidence, the reviewed summary is docs/integrity-fixes-closeout-2026-09-16.md
/.agent-contexts/integrity-audit-*/
/.agent-contexts/integrity-audit-*.log
/.agent-contexts/integrity-fixes-*/
# agent-kernel runtime state (session checkpoints, message blobs)
/.agent-kernel/
# WorkBuddy AI project data (session memory, logs)
/.workbuddy-ai/
# 2026-09-16 closeout scan: raw report + probe output stay local; the reviewed
# summary is docs/integrity-fixes-closeout-2026-09-16.md
/.agent-contexts/integrity-scan-*/
# 2026-09-21 TF-0229 mechanism round: raw probes, captured tsbx logs and the
# sandbox session dirs stay local as machine evidence. The reviewed summary is
# docs/tf0229-evidence-chain-2026-09-21.md; the readings live in TF-0229 /
# TF-0231 node evidence. Runtime copies of the sandbox binaries are purged
# (see that dir's runtime-purge.txt for how to rebuild them).
/.agent-contexts/tf0229-*/
/.agent-contexts/tf0229-*.log
# 2026-09-21 TF-0231 注入判据定位：三平台产物、判别探针、同会话矩阵与 tsbx 日志
# 都保留在本地。结论在 docs/tf0231-injection-discriminator-2026-09-21.md，
# 产物指纹在该目录的 artifact-sha256.txt。
/.agent-contexts/tf0231-*/
# 2026-09-17/18 absorption plan: the planning proposal draft and the per-round
# node-development proposal copies stay local. The applied copies live in
# .agent-workbench/task-forest/proposals/, and the readings live in node
# evidence + docs (see docs/absorption-progress-2026-09-18.md).
/.agent-contexts/absorption-plan-*/
/.agent-contexts/nodes-dev-*/
# 2026-09-21 read-only forest inspection (todos, validate, check-landing, git state).
# The findings went into .workbuddy/memory/2026-09-21.md; nothing here needs to be tracked.
/.agent-contexts/tf-inspect-*/
/.agent-contexts/todo-current.json

# Agent skills are third-party content vendored from `assistant-ui/skills` and
# recorded in `skills-lock.json` (which stays tracked). Two copies had been
# committed at `agent/skills/` and `.agents/skills/`, and `.claude/skills/<name>`
# are local junctions into `.agents/skills/<name>` — git followed those junctions
# and committed 78 more files that were byte-identical to the junction target.
# Keep the whole skill tree local and reinstall from the lock file when needed.
/agent/skills/
/.agents/skills/
/.claude/skills/
# context-rot footprint hook output (`install-hooks` writes footprints.jsonl
# here). Local observation data; the installer itself recommends ignoring it.
/.context-rot/

# docs/ holds the project's own record, but most of it is point-in-time working
# artifact. Only these stay in history:
#   decisions/  the ADR set — the authority
#   handoff/    one record per relay round: what changed, the evidence readings,
#     the repro commands, and what was deliberately NOT done. It is the only
#     artifact that lets the next operator continue the round on another
#     machine, so it ships — whitelisted BY DIRECTORY on purpose. The old
#     per-file whitelist is what let the 2026-09-25 handoff report sit ignored
#     and uncommitted while the round it described looked finished (ADR-0020,
#     "有用未传"). A directory cannot drift file by file.
#   user/       retired Helmor guide (bannered as a record)
#   fable-brief/  linked from ADR-0010, ADR-0016 and docs/user/README.md
#   perf/       phase1-trace-summary.json is deliberately whitelisted above
#   assets/     README / documentation illustrations (outcome, ADR-0020)
#   reicon-icons.md  referenced by AGENTS.md
#   fit-ledger.md    referenced by the shipped packages/workbench/README.md
#   phase4-human-usage-window-2026-09-22.md  the operating guide for the one
#     remaining human gate; ADR-0019 calls it durable and re-runnable, so
#     untracking it would make that gate unreproducible from the repo (P4).
# Everything else (dated reports, evidence dumps, closeout logs) stays local.
# After adding a doc, run `bun run check:upload-surface`: it fails on anything
# that is neither uploaded nor explicitly accepted as local-only (ADR-0020).
/docs/*
!/docs/decisions/
!/docs/handoff/
!/docs/user/
!/docs/fable-brief/
!/docs/perf/
!/docs/assets/
!/docs/reicon-icons.md
!/docs/fit-ledger.md
!/docs/phase4-human-usage-window-2026-09-22.md
!/docs/engineering-defect-localization-and-qa-plan-2026-09-24.md

# TF-0194 window round: the per-branch prompt scratch and the three driver
# scripts are working state. The round's curated readings stay tracked
# (README.md, shown-state.json, t1-baseline.json).
/.agent-contexts/tf0194-window/prompts/
/.agent-contexts/tf0194-window/serve.ts
/.agent-contexts/tf0194-window/step.ts
/.agent-contexts/tf0194-window/window.ts

# Evidence ledger (TF-0274). Readings and the claim registry are tracked — that is
# the whole point: a number nobody else can recompute is not evidence. The raw
# outputs they digest are process evidence per ADR-0020 and stay local.
/evidence/raw/

